<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="commentary" data-rev="0">
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">data</span> content/commentary/en.json; content/README.md (modified)</summary><div class="pl-card">The English template file: at least three unconditional lines for each of the twelve play event kinds, plus context sets for goals, fouls, cards, repeats, penalties, kick-offs, half-time, and full time. The modder reference documents the set shape, the conditions, the placeholders, and the selection order.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>content/</td><td>+305</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/commentary/mod.rs, templates.rs, context.rs, render.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The commentator: a fail-closed loader with garde validators, the match situation (minute band, score state, form, repeat count), a placeholder fill that refuses an unfilled token, and a selection that prefers the most specific set and does not repeat a line for a kind inside ten minutes of play. It consumes no engine random draw.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>crates/engine/src/commentary</td><td>+680</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/sim.rs, rules/mod.rs, team.rs, lib.rs, data/mod.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">Goal events name the last kicker, and restart and kick-off events name the taker. The last kicker is cleared at every dead ball, so the snapshot layout is unchanged. Teams keep player names, and EngineEventKind gains ALL and code().</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine/src</td><td>+65 / -5</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> crates/engine/tests/commentary.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The four criteria: every kind names its player and club; five same-kind events in ten minutes give three or more distinct lines; a late equaliser and a rout read as such; the seed-42 match leaves no placeholder unfilled and uses no fallback. The loader refusals are tested too.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>crates/engine/tests</td><td>+260</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">contract</span> crates/protocol/src/event.rs, lib.rs; docs/reference/protocol.md</summary><div class="pl-card">The event message gains an optional commentary field. Version 2 stands under the recorded additive-field judgement. The reference names the field and the new player.id meanings on goal and restart events.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/protocol and docs</td><td>+30 / -1</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">cli</span> crates/engine-cli/src/content.rs, stream_run.rs, bench.rs, record.rs, serve.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The commentary file loads with the other content. The shared match driver builds one commentator per match and attaches a line to every play event, so the socket, the fixture, and events.jsonl all carry it.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine-cli</td><td>+39 / -2</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R1 · Lines repeat and read as canned</div><div class="callout-body">A match has about 40 throw-ins and each kind starts with three unconditional lines. No line repeats for the same kind within ten minutes while the pool allows it. The rotation start comes from the seed. The file grows without code changes.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R2 · A goal or restart event carries no player</div><div class="callout-body">The engine now names the last kicker on a goal and the taker on a restart. The last kicker is cleared at every dead ball, so snapshots are unchanged. A unit test pins the invariant.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R3 · A strict reader refuses the new field</div><div class="callout-body">The only Rust reader, both producers, and the document test change in one commit. The page ignores unknown fields.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R4 · New event kinds from the tactics slice need lines</div><div class="callout-body">The loader requires three unconditional lines for every kind in EngineEventKind::ALL. A new kind fails the content test until someone writes its lines.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R5 · Per-tick processor time moves</div><div class="callout-body">About 400 lines per match against about 280,000 ticks. Step 1 records a baseline at the commit where implementation starts, and step 12 compares against it.</div></aside>
  </div>
  <details class="pl-revs"><summary>0 prior revisions</summary><ul></ul></details>
